sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant R as Reseller server
    participant API as POST /merchant/v1/validate/player
    participant G as ip_guard (2 counters)
    participant V as merchants.validate
    participant P as integrations.player_check
    participant B as SupplierBreaker (Redis)
    participant C as Redis cache (300s)
    participant S as G2B / Waxpeer
    participant DB as Postgres

    R->>API: POST {sku_id, player_id, server_id} (signed — body, never a URL)
    Note over R,API: player_id is the reseller's END CUSTOMER's -- transit only,<br/>never in a query string, never in a log line (only hash_short)
    API->>API: merchant_auth: HMAC + freshness + merchant-api IP counter (600/60s)
    API->>G: guard_ip("merchant-validate") 120/60s per ADDRESS
    API->>G: charge_merchant_quota(merchant_id) 120/60s per MERCHANT
    Note over G: two axes because the quota being rationed is a SUPPLIER's,<br/>and a reseller spends that per account, not per egress node
    alt over either
        G-->>R: 429 problem+json + Retry-After
    end

    API->>V: check_player(sku_id, player_id, server_id)
    V->>DB: SELECT products.id, products.required_fields,<br/>skus.visible_b2b, brands.visible_b2b WHERE skus.id = ?
    Note over V,DB: scoped exactly as /catalog is -- a SKU they cannot see<br/>is not checkable, so this cannot enumerate withheld SKUs
    alt no row
        V-->>R: 404 item_unavailable reason=unknown_sku
    else not visible_b2b (SKU or brand)
        V-->>R: 404 item_unavailable reason=not_b2b_visible
    end

    V->>V: product_is_checkable(required_fields)?
    alt no field declares check.provider
        V-->>R: 200 {status: "unsupported"} -- permanent — order without a check
        Note over V,R: NOT "valid" (that would approve nothing on purpose) and<br/>NOT a 404 (that would read as "no such SKU")
    end

    V->>P: check_player_for_product(product_id, ...)
    P->>C: GET playercheck:*:<hash>
    alt cache hit
        C-->>R: 200 the stored verdict, unchanged and uncaveated
        Note over C,R: a cached answer is still our best answer —<br/>a "this was cached" flag would only invite distrust of a good one
    end
    P->>DB: resolve g2b game_code from sku_supplier_mapping
    alt no active mapping, or two distinct codes
        P-->>R: 200 {status: "error"} + player_check_no_game_mapping<br/>/ player_check_ambiguous_game_code
    end
    P->>B: is_open()?
    alt circuit open
        B-->>R: 200 {status: "error"} -- the call is skipped, ~15s sooner
    end

    P->>DB: ROLLBACK (release the pool connection BEFORE the round trip)
    P->>S: checkPlayerId / steam-topup/validate
    alt transport or HTTP failure
        P->>B: record_failure()
        P-->>R: 200 {status: "error"}
    else 200 with a verdict we do NOT recognise
        P-->>R: 200 {status: "error"} + player_check_unrecognised_verdict
        Note over P,R: the mirror rule: an unreadable answer must not become<br/>"invalid", or a renamed field tells every customer they mistyped
    else recognised verdict
        P->>C: SET the verdict, 300s (verdicts only -- an error is never cached)
        P-->>R: 200 {status: "valid"|"invalid", name}
    end
